Template: anchorage/remove-config
Type: boolean
Default: true
_Description: Delete Anchorage's saved logins, backups and settings?
 This beta of Anchorage is being removed. Its folder /etc/anchorage holds
 the logins saved for network shares, the backups of /etc/fstab and
 Anchorage's settings.
 .
 /etc/fstab itself is not changed: drives, binds and network shares that
 Anchorage added keep working without it.

Template: anchorage/remove-config-in-use
Type: boolean
Default: false
_Description: Delete Anchorage's saved logins, backups and settings?
 This beta of Anchorage is being removed. Its folder /etc/anchorage holds
 the logins saved for network shares, the backups of /etc/fstab and
 Anchorage's settings.
 .
 ${COUNT} network share(s) in /etc/fstab still use a login saved there.
 If you delete it, those shares will stop mounting until you add their
 logins again (or remove them from /etc/fstab).
 .
 /etc/fstab itself is not changed.
